// This node's own checkpoint: a match expression's result, once its own
// closing POP retires the synthetic "subject" local, is exposed as a named
// local's own value — the fused local/stack model has no separate cell to
// push for a genuine consumer to read (bytecode-translation-problems.md,
// "RETURN can return a named local"). RETURN and SET_GLOBAL already share
// this fold check with the rest of the peek family; PRINT and DEFINE_GLOBAL
// are the two shapes this probe adds:
//
// line 1: `var n = ...` at script scope is a global DEFINITION
// (DEFINE_GLOBAL), not a local — this is the shape that needs
// DEFINE_GLOBAL's own fold check; with no fix, emission fails loudly
// before this line's PRINT is ever reached.
// line 2: the match's result is printed with nothing in between to declare
// a real local first — the shape that needs PRINT's own fold check.
// line 3: the match's result flows into a global assignment (`g = ...`,
// SET_GLOBAL), already fold-aware.
var n = match 1 { case _ => 5 }; print n;
print match 1 { case 1 => "a" case _ => "b" };
var g = 0; g = match 1 { case 1 => "a" case _ => "b" }; print g;
